#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""openswarm — Claude plans, Codex / OpenCode Go / DeepSeek execute.

Cursor CLI is an opt-in executor (`--backend cursor`); it is not in the automatic routing order.
The Antigravity CLI is an opt-in executor too (`--backend agy`, alias `--backend gemini`); it is not in
the automatic routing order either.
Pi coding agent is an opt-in executor (`--backend pi`); it is not in the automatic routing order either.

Subcommands:
  probe            discover models, plans, quotas -> $OPENSWARM_HOME/state.json (default ~/.claude/openswarm)
  status           human summary of state + recommended concurrency
  route            pick backend/model/effort for a task profile (JSON out)
  run              route + execute in an isolated git worktree, record ledger (JSON out)
  compare          run the same card on two executors and record a best-of-two comparison
  regress          run or compare a regression-card suite
  review           cross-family read-only review of a finished run
  consult          ask multiple executors the same question in read-only mode
  lessons          preview, propose, and escalate executor lessons
  patterns         propose reusable patterns and check active patterns for retirement
  lane             manage long-lived Codex app-server / Cursor ACP / Pi RPC executor lanes
  fleet            inspect hosts and forward openswarm commands over local / SSH / instabox transports
  batch            queue task cards across fleet hosts and collect their branches
  verify-remote    verify a fleet run on another host in a temporary worktree
  bus              initialize or inspect a GitHub issue bus repository
  bus-worker       run the reference GitHub issue bus executor
  watch            stream actionable events (progress, risk, stalls) for one or more runs
  runs / report    snapshot of recent runs / compact scheduled check-in
  resume           recover active runs and recent results after planner restart
  retro            weekly fleet retrospective (Markdown report + JSON summary)
  stop             terminate a run (partial work is still committed to its branch)
  ingest-claude    record Claude plan usage (from statusline JSON on stdin, or flags)
  ledger           show recent runs or ingest GitHub PR results

Local data sources and credentials are documented in README.md ("What openswarm reads").
Nothing that reads another tool's login/auth file is enabled by default.
"""
